#: data/knowledge.xml:67
msgid "Measurement of an amount of matter."
msgstr "Midía d'una cantidá de materia"

#: data/knowledge.xml:70
msgid "Matter"
msgstr "Materia"

#: data/knowledge.xml:71
msgid "All that takes up space and has mass."
msgstr "Tolo qu'ocupa un espaciu y tien una masa"

#: data/knowledge.xml:74
msgid "Phase"
msgstr "Fase"

#: data/knowledge.xml:75
msgid ""
"Through chemical composition and physical attributes, homogeneous portion of "
"matter that separated from its environment in its expansion through a "
"surface."
msgstr ""
"En composición química y atributos físicos, parte homoxénea d'una sustancia "
"que pue separtase d'un entornu na so espansión a través d'una superficie."

#: data/knowledge.xml:78
msgid "Accuracy and precision"
msgstr "Esautitú y precisión"

#: data/knowledge.xml:79
msgid ""
"Expressed through standard deviation: Values given over accidental errors."
msgstr ""
"Esprésase a través de la desviación estándar como los valores daos sobre "
"erros accidentales."

#: data/knowledge.xml:82
msgid "Correctness"
msgstr "Correición"

#: data/knowledge.xml:83
msgid "Values given over accidental errors."
msgstr "Valores daos sobre erros accidentales."

#: data/knowledge.xml:86
msgid "SI-Unit"
msgstr "Unidá del SI"

#: data/knowledge.xml:87
msgid "Measurement unit using International Symbols."
msgstr "Unidá de midía qu'usa símbolos internacionales"

#: data/knowledge.xml:90
msgid "Significant figures"
msgstr "Díxitos significativos"

#: data/knowledge.xml:91
msgid "The number of digits which are meaningful in a number."
msgstr "El númberu de díxitos d'un númberu que son significativos."

#: data/knowledge.xml:94
msgid "Standard deviation"
msgstr "Desviación estándar"

#: data/knowledge.xml:95
msgid "An amount with which the precision of a measurement can be estimated."
msgstr ""

#: data/knowledge.xml:98
msgid "Suspension"
msgstr "Suspensión"

#: data/knowledge.xml:99
msgid "Heterogeneous mix consisting of a liquid and solid matter."
msgstr ""
"Amestadura heteroxénea que consta d'un llíquidu y d'una materia sólida."

#: data/knowledge.xml:102
msgid "Alloys"
msgstr "Combinación"

#: data/knowledge.xml:103
msgid "Pure matter consisting of multiple elements in a set ratio."
msgstr "Materia pura que consiste en dellos elementos nuna mesma proporción."

#: data/knowledge.xml:106
msgid "Alpha rays"
msgstr "Rayos alfa"

#: data/knowledge.xml:107
msgid ""
"Rays consisting of alpha particles, consisting of two protons and two "
"neutrons that are emitted from the Atoms of certain radioactive elements."
msgstr ""
"Rayos compuestos por partícules alfa, que consisten en dos protones y dos "
"neutrones que son emitíos por los átomos de ciertos elementos radiactivos."

#: data/knowledge.xml:110 data/knowledge.xml:123 data/knowledge.xml:130
#: data/knowledge.xml:138 data/knowledge.xml:215 data/knowledge.xml:222
#: data/knowledge.xml:231
msgid "Atom"
msgstr "Átomu"

#: data/knowledge.xml:111
msgid ""
"Atoms are chemically inseparable and building blocks of matter. Atoms of one "
"kind are called an Element."
msgstr ""
"Los átomos son químicamente insepartables y constituyen bloques de materia. "
"Los átomos d'una mesma triba denómense «elementu»."

#: data/knowledge.xml:114 data/knowledge.xml:211 data/knowledge.xml:223
#: data/knowledge.xml:232 data/knowledge.xml:240
msgid "Electron"
msgstr "Electrón"

#: data/knowledge.xml:115 data/knowledge.xml:219 data/knowledge.xml:233
msgid "Proton"
msgstr "Protón"

#: data/knowledge.xml:116 data/knowledge.xml:224 data/knowledge.xml:228
msgid "Neutron"
msgstr "Neutrón"

#: data/knowledge.xml:120
msgid "Atomic nucleus"
msgstr "Núcleu atómicu"

#: data/knowledge.xml:121
msgid ""
"The small, positively-charged center of an Atom, in which Protons and "
"Neutrons are found."
msgstr ""
"El pequeñu centru d'un átomu, cargáu positivamente, nel que puen atopase los "
"protones y los neutrones."

#. i18n: ectx: property (text), item, widget (KComboBox, KCB_x)
#. i18n: ectx: property (text), item, widget (KComboBox, KCB_y)
#: data/knowledge.xml:127 src/elementdataviewer.cpp:228
#: src/kalziumgradienttype.cpp:290 src/plotsetupwidget.ui:59
#: src/plotsetupwidget.ui:380
msgid "Atomic Mass"
msgstr "Masa atómica"

#: data/knowledge.xml:128
msgid ""
"Mass of an atom, taken on a scale where the mass of a carbon atom is 12u. In "
"elements that consist of different isotopes the mid-range mass of the "
"isotope mix is given."
msgstr ""
"Masa d'un átomu tomada d'una escala au la masa del átomu de carbonu ye 12u. "
"Pa los elementos que consisten n'estremaos isótopos, proporciónase la masa "
"media de l'amestadura d'isótopos."

#: data/knowledge.xml:135 data/knowledge.xml:145 data/knowledge.xml:152
#: data/knowledge.xml:159 data/knowledge.xml:166 data/knowledge.xml:173
#: data/knowledge.xml:183 data/knowledge.xml:192 data/knowledge.xml:201
msgid "Isotope"
msgstr "Isótopu"

#: data/knowledge.xml:136
msgid ""
"Isotopes are forms of a chemical element whose nuclei have the same atomic "
"number, Z, but different atomic masses, A. The word isotope, meaning at the "
"same place, comes from the fact that all isotopes of an element are located "
"at the same place on the periodic table."
msgstr ""
"Los isótopos son formes d'un elementu químicu que tien un núcleu col mesmu "
"númberu atómicu Z, pero estremada masa atómica, A. La pallabra \"isótopu\", "
"que significa \"nel mesmu llugar\", deriva del fechu de que los isótopos "
"d'un elementu tan asitiaos nel mesmu llugar de la tabla periódica."

#: data/knowledge.xml:142
msgid "Spin"
msgstr "Espín"

#: data/knowledge.xml:143
msgid ""
"The spin is an intrinsic angular momentum associated with microscopic "
"particles. It is a purely quantum mechanical phenomenon without any analogy "
"in classical mechanics. Whereas classical angular momentum arises from the "
"rotation of an extended object, spin is not associated with any rotating "
"internal masses, but is intrinsic to the particle itself."
msgstr ""
"L'espín ye un momentu angular intrínsecu venceyáu a partícules "
"microscópiques. Ye un fenómenu dafechu mecanicocuánticu ensin nenguna "
"analoxía na mecánica clásica. Demientres que'l momentu angular clásicu "
"provien de la rotación d'un oxetu estendíu, l'espín nun ta venceyáu con "
"nenguna masa interna en rotación, sinon que ye intrínsecu a la propia "
"partícula."

#: data/knowledge.xml:149 src/detailinfodlg.cpp:345
msgid "Magnetic Moment"
msgstr "Momentu magnéticu"

#: data/knowledge.xml:150
msgid ""
"The magnetic moment of an object is a vector relating the aligning torque in "
"a magnetic field experienced by the object to the field vector itself. It is "
"measured in units of the nuclear magneton µ[sub]n[/sub]=(5.0507866 ± "
"0.0000017) 10[sup]-27[/sup] JT[sup]-1[/sup]"
msgstr ""

#: data/knowledge.xml:156
msgid "Decay Mode"
msgstr "Mou de desintegración"

#: data/knowledge.xml:157
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The decay mode describes a particular way a particle decays. For "
#| "radioactive decay (the decay of nuclides) the decay modes are:[br] -> "
#| "alpha decay (emission of a Helium-4 nucleus).[br] -> &#946;[sup]-[/sup] "
#| "decay (emission of an electron)[br] -> &#946;[sup]+[/sup] decay (emission "
#| "of a positron) [br] -> electron capture (EC) [br] -> proton emission [br] "
#| "-> spontaneous fission [br] Typically one decay mode predominates for a "
#| "particular nuclide."
msgid ""
"The decay mode describes a particular way a particle decays. For radioactive "
"decay (the decay of nuclides) the decay modes are:[br] -> alpha decay "
"(emission of a Helium-4 nucleus).[br] -> ß[sup]-[/sup] decay (emission of an "
"electron)[br] -> ß[sup]+[/sup] decay (emission of a positron) [br] -> "
"electron capture (EC) [br] -> proton emission [br] -> spontaneous fission "
"[br] Typically one decay mode predominates for a particular nuclide."
msgstr ""
"El mou de desintegración describe una forma particular de desintegración "
"d'una partícula. Pa la desintegración radiactiva (de los núclidos), los "
"modos de desintegración son:[br] -> desintegración alfa (emisión d'un núcleu "
"d'Heliu-4).[br] -> desintegración &#946;[sup]-[/sup] (emisión d'un ellectrón)"
"[br] -> desintegración &#946;[sup]+[sup] (emisión d'un positrón)[br] -> "
"captura d'un ellectrón (CE)[br] -> emisión d'un protón[br] -> fisión "
"espontánea[br] Típicamente, un mou de desintegración predomina pa un núclido "
"particular."

#: data/knowledge.xml:163
msgid "Decay Energy"
msgstr "Enerxía de desintegración"

#: data/knowledge.xml:164
msgid "The decay energy is the energy released by a nuclear decay."
msgstr ""
"La enerxía de desintegración ye la enerxía lliberada demientres una "
"desintegración nuclear."

#: data/knowledge.xml:170
msgid "Nuclides"
msgstr "Núclidos"

#: data/knowledge.xml:171
msgid "[i]see isotopes[/i]"
msgstr "[i]ver isótopos[/i]"

#: data/knowledge.xml:174 data/knowledge.xml:180 data/knowledge.xml:193
#: data/knowledge.xml:203
msgid "Isotone"
msgstr "Isotonu"

#: data/knowledge.xml:175 data/knowledge.xml:184 data/knowledge.xml:194
#: data/knowledge.xml:198
msgid "Nuclear Isomer"
msgstr "Isómeru nuclear"

#: data/knowledge.xml:176 data/knowledge.xml:185 data/knowledge.xml:189
#: data/knowledge.xml:202
msgid "Isobars"
msgstr "Isobaros"

#: data/knowledge.xml:181
msgid "Two nuclides are isotones if they have the same number N of neutrons."
msgstr "Dos núclidos son isotonos si tienen el mesmu númberu de neutrones, N."

#: data/knowledge.xml:190
msgid ""
"Isobars are nuclides having the same mass number, i.e. sum of protons plus "
"neutrons."
msgstr ""
"Los isobaros son núclidos que tienen la mesma masa atómica (la suma de "
"protones y neutrones)."

#: data/knowledge.xml:199
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "A nuclear isomer is a metastable or isomeric state of an atom caused by "
#| "the excitation of a proton or neutron in its nucleus so that it requires "
#| "a change in spin before it can release its extra energy. They decay to "
#| "lower energy states of the nuclide through two isomeric transitions:[br] -"
#| "> &#947;- emission (emission of a high-energy photon)[br] -> internal "
#| "conversion (the energy is used to ionize the atom)[br] Contrast this with "
#| "the definition of a chemical isomer, the more common use of the word. "
#| "Also contrast with the meaning of isotope, in which the difference is the "
#| "number of neutrons in the nucleus. Metastable isomers of a particular "
#| "atom are usually designated with an \"m\" (or, in the case of atoms with "
#| "more than one isomer, 2m, 3m, and so on). This designation is usually "
#| "placed after the atomic symbol and number of the atom (e.g., Co-58m), but "
#| "is sometimes placed as a superscript before (e.g., [sup]m[/sup]Co-58 or "
#| "[sup]58m[/sup]Co)."
msgid ""
"A nuclear isomer is a metastable or isomeric state of an atom caused by the "
"excitation of a proton or neutron in its nucleus so that it requires a "
"change in spin before it can release its extra energy. They decay to lower "
"energy states of the nuclide through two isomeric transitions:[br] -> γ- "
"emission (emission of a high-energy photon)[br] -> internal conversion (the "
"energy is used to ionize the atom)[br] Contrast this with the definition of "
"a chemical isomer, the more common use of the word. Also contrast with the "
"meaning of isotope, in which the difference is the number of neutrons in the "
"nucleus. Metastable isomers of a particular atom are usually designated with "
"an \"m\" (or, in the case of atoms with more than one isomer, 2m, 3m, and so "
"on). This designation is usually placed after the atomic symbol and number "
"of the atom (e.g., Co-58m), but is sometimes placed as a superscript before "
"(e.g., [sup]m[/sup]Co-58 or [sup]58m[/sup]Co)."
msgstr ""
"Un isómeru nuclear ye un estáu metaestable o isoméricu d'un átomu causáu "
"pola escitación d'un protón o d'un neutrón nel so núcleu, de mou que requier "
"un cambéu nel espín enantes de que pueda lliberar la so enerxía estra. "
"Decaen a estaos más baxos d'enerxía del núclido a través de dos transiciones "
"isomériques:[br] -> &#947;- emisión (emisión d'un fotón d'alta enerxía)[br] -"
"> conversión interna (la enerxía úsase pa ionizar l'átomu)[br] Contraste "
"esto con la definición d'un isómeru químicu, que ye l'usu más común d'esta "
"pallabra. Contrástelo tamién col significáu d'isótopu, nel que la diferencia "
"ye'l númberu de neutrones del núcleu. Los isómeros metaestables d'un átomu "
"particular desígnesen usualmente con una «m» (o, nel casu d'átomos con más "
"d'un isómeru, 2m, 3m, etc.). Esta designación ponse normalmente tres el "
"símbolu y el númberu atómicu (por exemplu, Co-58m), anque delles vegaes "
"colócase como superíndice delantre de los mesmos (por exemplu., [sup]m[/sup]"
"Co-58 o [sup]58m[/sup]Co)."

#: data/knowledge.xml:207
msgid "Beta rays"
msgstr "Rayos beta"

#: data/knowledge.xml:208
msgid ""
"Rays consisting of electrons that are emitted from Atoms of radioactive "
"elements."
msgstr ""
"Rayos compuestos por ellectrones que son emitíos por átomos d'elementos "
"radiactivos."

